Dear Administrative Court,

I write further to the Order of the Hon. Mrs Justice Lieven dated 4 Decembe=
r 2025.

I respectfully provide the attached Clarification Note, which is submitted =
solely to assist the Court by setting out, in concise form:
The continuing nature of the administrative and safeguarding matters raised=
 in the claim;
The basis on which urgency arises; and
A new development occurring on 4 December 2025 concerning HMCTS=E2=80=99s lack of=
 internal record of the Judicial Review claim, which is directly relevant to=
 the issues of administrative handling.
=20

This Note is not a request to vary or challenge the Order, but is provided =
to ensure the Court has fully accurate and up-to-date information in accorda=
nce with its ongoing duties under the Equality Act 2010 and the Public Secto=
r Equality Duty, given my disabilities (autism and PTSD) and the safeguardin=
g concerns arising from the administrative silence and lack of participation=
 measures.

=20

For convenience, the full text of the Clarification Note is also set out be=
low the signature in the email body.

=20

Please confirm that the attached document will be placed on the Court file.

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

Claimant

AC-2025-LON-004293

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

Attachment:

Clarification_Note_with_Title_AC-2025-LON-004293.pdf

CLARIFICATION NOTE =E2=80=94 AC-2025-LON-004293

Filed: 4 December 2025

Claimant: Nadia Zahmoul

=20

1. Purpose

This Note responds to the Court=E2=80=99s Order of 4 December 2025, clarifying th=
at the urgency relates to ongoing administrative and safeguarding concerns, =
and referencing new developments arising on the same day.

=20

2. Continuing Nature of the Breaches

The Claim challenges current administrative failures:

=E2=80=A2 No logging or safeguarding of evidence submissions.

=E2=80=A2 No chain-of-custody records for the Imerman devices.

=E2=80=A2 Withdrawal of participation measures without determination.

=E2=80=A2 No disability adjustments or PSED engagement.

These breaches persist today.

=20

3. New Development on 4 December 2025

HMCTS Litigation Team confirmed they had no record of receiving the Judicia=
l Review claim and were unable to acknowledge service until the Claimant re-=
sent documents. This supports the Claimant=E2=80=99s case of ongoing administrativ=
e failures.

=20

4. Safeguarding and Disability Considerations

The Claimant, who is autistic and has PTSD, continues to experience deterio=
ration arising from administrative silence and lack of reasonable adjustment=
s. This raises immediate safeguarding and participation issues.

=20

5. Renewed Request

The Claimant respectfully renews her request that:
Permission not be determined on the papers; and
The matter be listed for an urgent oral hearing.
=20

6. Conclusion

This Note is provided to assist the Court and ensure accurate understanding=
 of the ongoing issues.

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20


